  "domain": "blockchain",
  "definition": "Distributed Ledger Technology (DLT) refers to a class of decentralised database protocols in which transaction records are replicated, shared, and synchronised across multiple networked nodes without a central administrator. Consensus mechanisms \u2014 such as proof-of-work, proof-of-stake, and Byzantine fault-tolerant protocols \u2014 ensure agreement on the canonical state of the ledger. DLT underpins blockchain networks, permissioned enterprise ledgers, and novel consensus architectures used in finance, supply chain, and identity management.",
